@startuml INA700_pi_architecture
' INA700 - the Pi's real system, as it runs at the station
' Author: Suraj Karki
' Course: INA700 - AI-based pick and place
'
' Read it left to right: the use cases depend on the ports in the middle,
' and the adapters on the right implement them. Nothing points the other
' way. That is what lets the Basler be swapped for a folder of photos
' without a single use case noticing, and tests/test_architecture.py fails
' the build if an import ever crosses the wrong way.
'
' One adapter per port: the one the pi profile actually builds. The mock
' detector, the file replay and the loopback robot
' exist in the repository for the tests, and none of them is in the cell,
' so none of them is in this picture.

title INA700 - the system that runs on the Raspberry Pi

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #333333
  FontSize 12
  BackgroundColor #FDF6E8
  BackgroundColor<<port>> #EAF2FB
  BackgroundColor<<use case>> #EFF6EC
  BackgroundColor<<value>> #F2F2EE
  BackgroundColor<<utility>> #F2F2EE
  BackgroundColor<<hardware>> #FBEAEA
}

package "application\n(use cases)" as APP {
  class VisionPipeline <<use case>>
  class CoordinateService <<use case>>
  class CycleController <<use case>>
  class RobotCommander <<use case>>
  class CompositeSelector <<use case>>
  class SharedState <<use case>>
}

package "ports\n(abstractions)" as PORTS {
  interface FrameSource <<port>>
  interface ObjectDetector <<port>>
  interface OrientationEstimator <<port>>
  interface ColourClassifier <<port>>
  interface SceneCalibrator <<port>>
  interface CoordinateMapper <<port>>
  interface ObjectSelector <<port>>
  interface RobotTransport <<port>>
  interface View <<port>>
}

package "adapters\n(the outside world)" as ADAPT {
  class Camera <<hardware>>
  class NcnnDetector
  class FittedOrientationEstimator
  class HsvColourClassifier
  class ArucoCalibrator
  class MutableHomographyMapper
  class TcpServerTransport <<hardware>>
  class TkView
  class ConsoleView
}

package "domain  (pure rules - no cv2, no numpy, no sockets)" as DOMAIN {
  class Detection <<value>>
  class DetectedObject <<value>>
  class MappedScene <<value>>
  class WorldPose <<value>>
  enum Shape
  enum Colour
  class geometry <<utility>>
  class area <<utility>>
}

package "infrastructure" as INFRA {
  class Container
  class ThreadSupervisor
  class config_loader <<utility>>
}

' --- use case  -->  port  <|..  adapter, one row each ------------------
VisionPipeline --> FrameSource
FrameSource <|.. Camera

VisionPipeline --> ObjectDetector
ObjectDetector <|.. NcnnDetector

VisionPipeline --> OrientationEstimator
OrientationEstimator <|.. FittedOrientationEstimator

VisionPipeline --> ColourClassifier
ColourClassifier <|.. HsvColourClassifier

VisionPipeline --> SceneCalibrator
SceneCalibrator <|.. ArucoCalibrator

CoordinateService --> CoordinateMapper
CoordinateMapper <|.. MutableHomographyMapper

CycleController --> ObjectSelector
ObjectSelector <|.. CompositeSelector

RobotCommander --> RobotTransport
RobotTransport <|.. TcpServerTransport

SharedState <-- View
View <|.. TkView
View <|.. ConsoleView

' --- inside the application layer --------------------------------------
CycleController --> RobotCommander
CycleController --> SharedState

' --- what each layer knows of the domain -------------------------------
VisionPipeline ..> Detection
CoordinateService ..> MappedScene
CoordinateService ..> WorldPose
CoordinateService ..> geometry
CompositeSelector ..> area
DetectedObject ..> WorldPose
Detection --> Shape
Detection --> Colour

' --- the composition root ----------------------------------------------
' Deliberately NOT drawn as arrows into every package: the composition
' root touches all of them, and nine more lines across the picture would
' hide the one relationship this diagram exists to show.
Container ..> config_loader : reads the profile through

note bottom of Container
  The composition root, and the only file
  that names a concrete class. It builds
  whichever adapter the profile names and
  hands them to the use cases; change one
  line of config and the same use cases run
  against different hardware, with nothing
  below here noticing.

  ThreadSupervisor then runs those use cases
  on the five threads - see pi-02-threads.
end note

note bottom of ArucoCalibrator
  Re-solves the homography from the marker's
  four corners on every frame, so a nudged
  camera corrects itself rather than quietly
  placing beside the object. Pixels per
  millimetre is never stored.
end note

@enduml
